WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:03.402
-We are joined right now by one
of my favorite people on Earth,

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:04.737
one of my favorite actors.

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:07.073
She's a very talented actor
who stars in the film

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:08.441
"Wander Darkly,"

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:10.376
which is in select theaters
and on demand today.

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:14.180
Here is Sienna Miller.
Ah, look at you.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:17.116
Come on.
I'm so happy to see you.

00:00:17.116 --> 00:00:19.084
-I'm so happy to see you.
-Look at how festive it is.

00:00:19.084 --> 00:00:21.721
-...festive.
It's so festive.

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:23.256
Everything is.

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:26.025
Is this -- are you in London?
Are you back in London?

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:27.727
-Lapland.

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:29.062
-Where?

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:31.897
-Lapland.
-What's that now?

00:00:31.897 --> 00:00:34.367
-That's where Father Christmas
lives, Lapland.

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:36.269
-I've never heard that.
That's not true.

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:37.970
I've never heard that.
-Are you kidding me?

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:39.672
You've never heard of Lapland?

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:41.307
-No, Lapland?
No, never.

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:43.676
North Pole?
-Right.

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:46.679
It's in English, it's potato,
potahto, tomato, tomahto.

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:47.980
-I love even the way
you said "right,"

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:49.482
you went right into
an American accent.

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:51.483
You go, "Right."
-Right. Right.

00:00:51.483 --> 00:00:55.054
-Right. Santa -- Santa Claus --
Father Christmas.

00:00:55.054 --> 00:00:57.122
-Father Christmas.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.122 --> 00:01:00.826
-I love Chri-- I want
to go to England in Christmas.

00:01:00.826 --> 00:01:02.595
I feel like it's the best place
for Christmas.

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:04.330
-It's pretty cozy right now.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:07.033
-How was your quarantine
in New York?

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:09.468
I heard that you were here.
-It was interesting.

00:01:09.468 --> 00:01:12.171
I mean, it was kind of --
initially it was fun.

00:01:12.171 --> 00:01:14.707
It was like a perpetual
snow day.

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:18.544
I liked that bit, it was like,
"Ooh, hunker down."

00:01:18.544 --> 00:01:20.513
And then it got repetitive.
-Yeah.

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:23.315
-And I'm not a natural teacher.
I really tried.

00:01:23.315 --> 00:01:25.151
I'm sure
you're in the same boat.

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:27.052
-Oh, my gosh.
I love teachers so much.

00:01:27.052 --> 00:01:28.788
I'm like, oh, my gosh.

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:32.492
I can't even imagine.
-I mean, those guys, yeah.

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.427
-How old is your daughter now,
is she 8?

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:36.895
-She's 8.
-Yeah, because Winnie's 7, yeah.

00:01:36.895 --> 00:01:39.599
You brought a video,
which I'm excited to show,

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:43.069
because you were having
fun with Marlowe.

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:44.737
What does she -- she has
a hoverboard?

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.572
How did you make this?
-She has a hoverboard,

00:01:46.572 --> 00:01:48.007
and we had some cardboard boxes

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:49.976
that had, at one point,
food in them.

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:52.345
And of course you get creative
when you have an only child

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:53.946
and it's lockdown.

00:01:53.946 --> 00:01:57.116
So we made the hoverboard
into a car.

00:01:57.116 --> 00:01:59.318
And I feel like
the mood of it

00:01:59.318 --> 00:02:01.854
is essentially the state of mind
that we've all been in

00:02:01.854 --> 00:02:03.589
in our family.
-Let's take a look.

00:02:03.589 --> 00:02:05.892
Here's Sienna and her daughter
having fun during quarantine.

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:07.093
Take a look.

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:10.363
-Yeah.

00:02:13.465 --> 00:02:15.034
Whoa, whoa!
[ Crash ]

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:17.936
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.936 --> 00:02:19.705
-She's okay, right? Yeah.

00:02:19.705 --> 00:02:21.207
-She's fine.
-That's so cute.

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:22.575
-They kind of got
a few laughs, yeah.

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:24.777
-Whew!
-Yeah.

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:27.146
-Sienna, before we talk about
"Wander Darkly,"

00:02:27.146 --> 00:02:30.183
I know you got to work with
the late Chadwick Boseman

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:32.051
on "21 Bridges."

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:33.753
We all miss him.

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:36.856
You recently in an article
told this story

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:39.592
about how he gave up
some of his salary

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:41.794
from that movie
to increase your salary,

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:45.464
because you weren't
being paid equally.

00:02:45.464 --> 00:02:47.466
I was just wondering,
could I hear the story?

00:02:47.466 --> 00:02:49.002
Like, how did that happen?

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:51.971
-It just feels like
an unprecedented thing

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:54.741
in Hollywood, in the town
that we work in.

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:56.175
-Yeah.

00:02:56.175 --> 00:02:58.478
-It's something that everybody
talks about,

00:02:58.478 --> 00:03:00.413
which is the pay disparity
between men and women,

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:02.181
and obviously there should be
one between me

00:03:02.181 --> 00:03:03.716
and "Black Panther,"

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:05.484
like I get it,
that's totally fine.

00:03:05.484 --> 00:03:07.753
But we were in a negotiation
to do this film,

00:03:07.753 --> 00:03:09.756
which I really
wanted to do.

00:03:09.756 --> 00:03:12.725
And I had a number in mind
that I felt was fair,

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:15.361
and the studio wouldn't meet
that number,

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:17.863
and Chadwick was not only
starring in this film

00:03:17.863 --> 00:03:19.732
but was also producing it.

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:22.801
And he donated
some of his salary

00:03:22.801 --> 00:03:24.870
to get me to the number
that I had asked for.

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:29.942
And never mentioned it, never
sort of asked for any thanks.

00:03:29.942 --> 00:03:33.479
I, of course, towards the end of
shooting with him approached him

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:36.348
and was just like, "What you did
was the most astounding thing

00:03:36.348 --> 00:03:38.551
that anyone has ever really done
for me in this town."

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:41.487
And it's so validating
and so generous

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:43.756
and so respectful
and dignified,

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:45.591
and just eternally grateful.

00:03:45.591 --> 00:03:47.493
And he said,

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:49.328
"You got paid what
you deserve to be paid."

00:03:49.328 --> 00:03:50.997
And that's it.
Like...

00:03:50.997 --> 00:03:52.965
-I love that you talked
about that,

00:03:52.965 --> 00:03:54.900
because people need
to bring up

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:58.737
that uncomfortable
conversation every time,

00:03:58.737 --> 00:04:01.440
until you don't need to have
that conversation any more.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:04.877
-I think other actors, as well.
That was part of the reason

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:07.312
that I said it, because I think
other actors I've spoken to

00:04:07.312 --> 00:04:10.583
about it -- not publicly,
but before I said it --

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:12.584
were really inspired by that.

00:04:12.584 --> 00:04:14.987
I think it's a wakeup call
for a lot of people to see

00:04:14.987 --> 00:04:17.090
that kind of act of generosity,

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:19.358
and maybe think about
their own behavior.

00:04:19.358 --> 00:04:21.694
And it starts with one person
doing one thing, you know?

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:24.664
That's how change happens,
and he was remarkable.

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:26.632
-I love it.
I want to talk about

00:04:26.632 --> 00:04:28.334
your new movie,
"Wander Darkly."

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:31.237
This is a really beautiful film.

00:04:31.237 --> 00:04:35.541
It premiered at Sundance
earlier this year, and...

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:37.543
I don't know if I've ever seen
a movie quite like this.

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:40.212
How do you set this up?

00:04:40.212 --> 00:04:41.714
-It's a hard one to talk about.

00:04:41.714 --> 00:04:44.283
It's basically a couple
who just had a baby.

00:04:44.283 --> 00:04:46.419
Me and Diego Luna,
who's the sweetest man.

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:48.120
-I love Diego Luna.
He's great.

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:49.588
-I know.
-He's really fun.

00:04:49.588 --> 00:04:51.190
-He's the best.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.592
And we're not getting on,
we've had a new baby,

00:04:53.592 --> 00:04:56.495
surprise, surprise,
it's like things are difficult.

00:04:56.495 --> 00:04:58.765
We get into -- yep.

00:04:58.765 --> 00:05:00.933
We get into a car accident,

00:05:00.933 --> 00:05:03.569
and my character thinks
she died.

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:05.204
So it's kind of on this journey.

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:08.240
He's the only person that
can see her, and we go back

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:10.143
to the inception
of our relationship --

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:11.844
I know it's confusing.
-No.

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:13.378
-And we kind of
go through the moments

00:05:13.378 --> 00:05:16.983
where we went wrong and we sort
of unpick those moments.

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:19.618
Like, the pivot moments where
something happened

00:05:19.618 --> 00:05:21.854
that kind of put us
on the wrong track.

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:24.957
That was what was beautiful.
But it's very surreal.

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:26.859
It's very dream-like.

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:29.962
-How was it like seeing
it with an audience?

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:33.232
-It was amazing, because
it was like the last kind of

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:35.701
collective experience
that I had.

00:05:35.701 --> 00:05:37.236
It was like a snot fest.

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:39.171
Everybody was crying
and sharing tissues.

00:05:39.171 --> 00:05:41.173
It was probably
a super spreader event.

00:05:41.173 --> 00:05:43.676
-That was the original title.

00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:45.678
-"Snot Fest"?
-"Snot Fest," yeah.

00:05:45.678 --> 00:05:47.713
They changed --
I'm happy that changed it

00:05:47.713 --> 00:05:50.583
because I think the title you
have now is much, much better.

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:52.418
It's more romantic
and more emotional.

00:05:52.418 --> 00:05:55.288
But they were considering
"Snot Fest" for a long time.

00:05:55.288 --> 00:05:57.990
-Sundance is so fun as well.
It was great.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:59.725
-I want to show
everyone a clip.

00:05:59.725 --> 00:06:02.562
Here is Sienna Miller
in "Wander Darkly."

00:06:02.562 --> 00:06:04.930
Take a look.

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:07.700
-You weren't there with Ellie.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:10.302
Where do you go?
What happens to you?

00:06:10.302 --> 00:06:12.071
You just -- you get scared
and then what?

00:06:12.071 --> 00:06:14.440
You just -- you disappear?

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:17.409
-You concussed.
That's it.

00:06:17.409 --> 00:06:19.111
-No.

00:06:19.111 --> 00:06:21.214
I died. I can step
into traffic now,

00:06:21.214 --> 00:06:23.282
it wouldn't matter.
-Hey!

00:06:23.282 --> 00:06:26.318
Hey.

00:06:26.318 --> 00:06:27.653
It's okay.

00:06:27.653 --> 00:06:29.054
-What is this, like, purgatory?

00:06:29.054 --> 00:06:31.557
What's --
what's happening to me?

00:06:31.557 --> 00:06:33.826
-Just hold on to me.
Hmm?

00:06:37.596 --> 00:06:39.465
[ Horn honks ]

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:41.167
-Sienna Miller,
"Wander Darkly"

00:06:41.167 --> 00:06:44.103
is in select theaters
and on demand today.

00:06:44.103 --> 00:06:46.071
"Wander Darkly."
Thank you so much

00:06:46.071 --> 00:06:47.973
for being here, buddy.

00:06:47.973 --> 00:06:50.476
Hug the baby and I hope to
see you soon, pal.

00:06:50.476 --> 00:06:52.345
Stay safe.
-Bye.

